  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary request path",
      "items": [
        "Customer and Admin browsers use the same React SPA and API client. Access tokens stay in memory; refresh tokens and current user are stored in localStorage for multi-tab refresh.",
        "NestJS exposes /api/v1 and applies CORS, Helmet, validation, rate limiting, JWT/session guards, role checks, and permission checks.",
        "Catalog, booking, pricing, payment, audit, operations, and mail capabilities remain modules in one API process; PostgreSQL is the durable system of record."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Seat, combo, and voucher consistency",
      "items": [
        "Redis NX locks with TTL reduce concurrent seat contention; PostgreSQL transactions authoritatively create bookings and seat holds.",
        "Combo selections are snapshotted at hold. Voucher code is an intent at hold; checkout serializes the booking, reprices, validates assignment/cinema/scope, and reserves redemption atomically.",
        "Idempotency keys, cursor-scoped list queries, database constraints, and expiry release paths protect retries and abandoned holds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Payment, reconciliation, and refund",
      "items": [
        "Checkout creates or reuses a SePay payment intent and QR using the server-confirmed total. SePay webhook matching is idempotent by gateway transaction ID.",
        "Matched payment confirms booking, sells seats, issues tickets, consumes voucher redemption, writes audit and MailOutbox in one transaction. Mismatches become REVIEW_REQUIRED for Admin reconciliation.",
        "Admin manual confirm and full booking refund are permission-protected and idempotent. Money transfer is outside the application; there is no automatic provider refund API."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Async delivery and operations",
      "items": [
        "MailOutbox is durable PostgreSQL state, not a Redis queue. A supervised Worker Thread claims rows, polls as fallback, retries SMTP failures, and is woken after commit.",
        "Booking expiry runs every minute, retention cleanup daily, and operational monitoring every minute in the API process. Health, Prometheus metrics, operations status, and optional Discord alerts expose runtime signals.",
        "The diagram reflects source commit e32066a. Worktree documentation and architecture artifacts are uncommitted; source references point to committed code at the pinned revision."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
